[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-334202"] :question/problem "Find the general solution of the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+4({y}^{′})^{2}-{y}^{′}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+4({y}^{′})^{2}-{y}^{′},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+4{p}^{2}-p.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(xp+4{p}^{2}-p)^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}+8p{p}^{′}-{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x+8p-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, which means at least one of the factors must be zero.\n\nThe general solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if ${p}^{′}=0.$ Then, $p$ is constant, say \n\n$$\np=c.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $p=c$ into $y=xp+4{p}^{2}-p,$ we get the general solution\n\n$$\ny=cx+4{c}^{2}-c.\n$$\n\nThis represents a family of straight lines, one line for each constant value of $c.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-334203/selection/6afaa8ae3f66c5976ef2421434728790fdb105d5d54b54a80994340a2f3a0f60" :answer/id #uuid "f0b66cc4-7f78-5e90-bcfd-5f782b836a8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=cx+{c}^{3}-2c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334203/selection/d199af4c0ea96f96b8e4c0d1c1b5690d838ee83205fd57cc363590c6bae8dcfd" :answer/id #uuid "654a8f27-f4f5-5530-a010-d1511f035c33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=cx+2{c}^{3}-2c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334203/selection/44781e612c30dbc4990af5d875b604e89138454420c845c1257f5b0bbcde827f" :answer/id #uuid "1258649e-a167-5438-a5ce-53173eb41888" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={c}^{3}x+{c}^{3}-2c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334203/selection/35c964e1b2d0f69a0ef6cac1536cc18005791d8cf7be2cd7ed62371e6b79e4ce" :answer/id #uuid "b4327a05-2572-52ce-b7a3-1c7e8e4e8354" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={c}^{2}x+{c}^{3}-2c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334203/selection/f04bc8d4acd40cae22e12f81f1d39c5acb12bebb81a3b95fb5daa9cf1fb85db3" :answer/id #uuid "019b0c8a-6b1b-520f-aff7-84c20fe95c36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=cx+{c}^{2}-2c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334203/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d67aab9-73af-5fc9-afac-f2cb1374dbea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334203/selection/6afaa8ae3f66c5976ef2421434728790fdb105d5d54b54a80994340a2f3a0f60" :answer-field/choices ["q-334203/selection/6afaa8ae3f66c5976ef2421434728790fdb105d5d54b54a80994340a2f3a0f60" "q-334203/selection/d199af4c0ea96f96b8e4c0d1c1b5690d838ee83205fd57cc363590c6bae8dcfd" "q-334203/selection/44781e612c30dbc4990af5d875b604e89138454420c845c1257f5b0bbcde827f" "q-334203/selection/35c964e1b2d0f69a0ef6cac1536cc18005791d8cf7be2cd7ed62371e6b79e4ce" "q-334203/selection/f04bc8d4acd40cae22e12f81f1d39c5acb12bebb81a3b95fb5daa9cf1fb85db3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334203" :question/id #uuid "284f78d5-711d-538b-9fce-2df62ab28f45" :question/math-academy-id "q-334203" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+({y}^{′})^{3}-2{y}^{′}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+({y}^{′})^{3}-2{y}^{′},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+{p}^{3}-2p.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(xp+{p}^{3}-2p)^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}+3{p}^{2}{p}^{′}-2{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x+3{p}^{2}-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, which means at least one of the factors must be zero.\n\nThe general solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if ${p}^{′}=0.$ Then, $p$ is constant, say \n\n$$\np=c.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $p=c$ into $y=xp+{p}^{3}-2p,$ we get the general solution\n\n$$\ny=cx+{c}^{3}-2c.\n$$\n\nThis represents a family of straight lines, one line for each constant value of $c.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334203/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aac5cb30-5659-547e-bedf-921f6c99067a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334203"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334210/selection/3b3e03a46362978fd9517836fde3e2689636f4696c4f102a615c1fbc8367d104" :answer/id #uuid "9b625242-479c-5943-9a7f-a03b4d67a566" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={c}^{2}x+\\frac{1}{c}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334210/selection/7d3e9534bc52a594ce901330bbe1b9a82d2538728a15edf3d5600ada782e04aa" :answer/id #uuid "9ea004f6-60a3-513e-83dc-66736662fe04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=cx+\\frac{1}{c}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334210/selection/808b7cd06c65942764c501c1f8e8f674a1d167ec49c95bc9362b9b859d8d0dbb" :answer/id #uuid "a0fc36dd-a482-549c-8fbc-83098f16eb1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={c}^{3}x+\\frac{1}{c}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334210/selection/15b4657625ed2d6348d1910905ba11a74d7f096abfae7cdc990a6b6d3be0d6a6" :answer/id #uuid "b13115f3-906f-5193-99bb-1a1901e0d883" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=cx+c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334210/selection/34916fcaabf2aa5ab974286488d7cfbf436d9e291863c355cab633ca547d2f88" :answer/id #uuid "89034d07-4829-5254-a3b9-249d0be9bea8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=cx+\\frac{1}{2c}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334210/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7efd41de-7ae6-5e88-8a98-2eda4a55bc39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334210/selection/7d3e9534bc52a594ce901330bbe1b9a82d2538728a15edf3d5600ada782e04aa" :answer-field/choices ["q-334210/selection/3b3e03a46362978fd9517836fde3e2689636f4696c4f102a615c1fbc8367d104" "q-334210/selection/7d3e9534bc52a594ce901330bbe1b9a82d2538728a15edf3d5600ada782e04aa" "q-334210/selection/808b7cd06c65942764c501c1f8e8f674a1d167ec49c95bc9362b9b859d8d0dbb" "q-334210/selection/15b4657625ed2d6348d1910905ba11a74d7f096abfae7cdc990a6b6d3be0d6a6" "q-334210/selection/34916fcaabf2aa5ab974286488d7cfbf436d9e291863c355cab633ca547d2f88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334210" :question/id #uuid "796e83ce-3077-5464-bc5e-9be0563f9d98" :question/math-academy-id "q-334210" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{′}},\\,{y}^{′}\\ne 0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{′}},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+\\frac{1}{p}.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={(xp+\\frac{1}{p})}^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}-\\frac{1}{{p}^{2}}{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x-\\frac{1}{{p}^{2}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, which means at least one of the factors must be zero.\n\nThe general solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if ${p}^{′}=0.$ Then, $p$ is constant, say \n\n$$\np=c,\n$$\n\nwith the restriction $c\\ne 0.$\n\nSubstituting $p=c$ into $y=xp+\\frac{1}{p},$ we get the general solution\n\n$$\ny=cx+\\frac{1}{c}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a family of straight lines, one line for each constant value of $c\\ne 0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334210/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aac5cb30-5659-547e-bedf-921f6c99067a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334210"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334453/selection/371e2684f52179d4deffe5011aa000ba0da439256ce72f5d926ea4471689d1ae" :answer/id #uuid "ce158720-1fc7-527b-87d0-908f5cce6c4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\\,x<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334453/selection/0d79e3619daea00d785985c55317cf9917717959fe439e6c4d729c9774382be1" :answer/id #uuid "cc15b468-9835-5cc4-9215-8542fefe13dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{4x},\\,x<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334453/selection/ebd813de9888e6195239377b6361c0a81eaf79bd6d147c82beb56edad8234c27" :answer/id #uuid "5aa110e4-0af4-5d43-9f6d-7aeda212de3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{x},\\,x>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334453/selection/7ad35fc6626875c9b4d564b7fbfb54a5d0c53f241d84f8e68ab4f3fd4609c808" :answer/id #uuid "922361bf-f167-5db2-a557-55ff20814d20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{x},\\,x<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334453/selection/99a8ea5008c384f2fcb456b9eeba3c4f82db67c7d7c83c6540110b72562fa23b" :answer/id #uuid "d08d2f5c-20e6-5fc4-8cdb-ff66476287ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2x},\\,x<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334453/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d95d9587-c73a-57a9-9174-9e73c054a9e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334453/selection/0d79e3619daea00d785985c55317cf9917717959fe439e6c4d729c9774382be1" :answer-field/choices ["q-334453/selection/371e2684f52179d4deffe5011aa000ba0da439256ce72f5d926ea4471689d1ae" "q-334453/selection/0d79e3619daea00d785985c55317cf9917717959fe439e6c4d729c9774382be1" "q-334453/selection/ebd813de9888e6195239377b6361c0a81eaf79bd6d147c82beb56edad8234c27" "q-334453/selection/7ad35fc6626875c9b4d564b7fbfb54a5d0c53f241d84f8e68ab4f3fd4609c808" "q-334453/selection/99a8ea5008c384f2fcb456b9eeba3c4f82db67c7d7c83c6540110b72562fa23b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334453" :question/id #uuid "19fc08b5-a70b-5aaf-9e22-7a42cd64e91f" :question/math-academy-id "q-334453" :question/problem "Find the singular solution to the following Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\sqrt{{y}^{′}},\\,{y}^{′}\\ge 0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A Clairaut differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $g$ is a differentiable function of ${y}^{′}.$\n\nTo solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\sqrt{{y}^{′}},\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+\\sqrt{p}.\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(xp+\\sqrt{p})^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}}{p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, so at least one factor must be zero.\n\nThe singular solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if $x+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}}=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute this into $y=xp+\\sqrt{p}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =xp+\\sqrt{p} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}})p+\\sqrt{p} \\\\  & =-\\frac{p}{2\\sqrt{p}}+\\sqrt{p} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{p}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the singular solution is given parametrically by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}} \\\\ y=\\frac{\\sqrt{p}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo eliminate $p,$ we first solve the first equation for $\\sqrt{p}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{p}=-\\frac{1}{2x}\n$$\n\nSince $x=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{p}},$ we must have $x<0.$\n\nNext, let's substitute this expression for $\\sqrt{p}$ into the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{\\sqrt{p}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{2x})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the explicit form of the singular solution is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{4x},\\,x<0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334453/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ddcff62-d052-51fd-9e2b-50358fa02de5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334453"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334457/selection/00c9154b9c60bd86b4afe7b714564d89301d0c7b060824ce6aba25a7965ed54d" :answer/id #uuid "424bbb5c-ce45-5484-ae8a-0478fc3620bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={x}^{2}\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334457/selection/bab7382b5772231e6f0581f7e7d01e34435b9fa127661a5d543181afccaf8906" :answer/id #uuid "fd027dd3-c6d7-5695-aa9b-fab52309c8d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334457/selection/aed43b7756e64ae9fddc5d522cf92cf60aab5edc846c6e5b138a4cdf02499fdf" :answer/id #uuid "e48d63ef-c40b-5f1d-ab43-32f57ab8213d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334457/selection/9c5f757b24fd16351bc7014abccb57bd4668f3b1c3e0ac982170459f08116dce" :answer/id #uuid "ca74d12f-cf40-58d9-b177-25f3b72dc052" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334457/selection/82ec7fa4ff0848092472afddbeeb4863a2f68c2c00d48b71c2924254acb821c0" :answer/id #uuid "0030d570-af4b-5827-8618-b37e058d369b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334457/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b84fb95-2319-5db5-bf51-b8e12537dc88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-334457/selection/aed43b7756e64ae9fddc5d522cf92cf60aab5edc846c6e5b138a4cdf02499fdf" :answer-field/choices ["q-334457/selection/00c9154b9c60bd86b4afe7b714564d89301d0c7b060824ce6aba25a7965ed54d" "q-334457/selection/bab7382b5772231e6f0581f7e7d01e34435b9fa127661a5d543181afccaf8906" "q-334457/selection/aed43b7756e64ae9fddc5d522cf92cf60aab5edc846c6e5b138a4cdf02499fdf" "q-334457/selection/9c5f757b24fd16351bc7014abccb57bd4668f3b1c3e0ac982170459f08116dce" "q-334457/selection/82ec7fa4ff0848092472afddbeeb4863a2f68c2c00d48b71c2924254acb821c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334457" :question/id #uuid "433e97c3-88c2-5dfc-9c81-2ab81a0cbb54" :question/math-academy-id "q-334457" :question/problem "Find the singular solution to the following Clairaut differential equation:\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{′}),\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le {y}^{′}\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A Clairaut differential equation has the form\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $g$ is a differentiable function of ${y}^{′}.$\n\nTo solve the Clairaut differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x{y}^{′}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwe start by setting\n$p={y}^{′}.$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation gives\n\n$$\ny=xp+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p).\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(xp+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p))^{′} \\\\ p & =p+x{p}^{′}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p){p}^{′} \\\\ 0 & ={p}^{′}(x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product on the right-hand side equals zero, so at least one factor must be zero.\n\nThe singular solution of the Clairaut differential equation is obtained if $x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p).\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute this into $y=xp+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =xp+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p))p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p) \\\\  & =p\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the singular solution is given parametrically by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p) \\\\ y=p\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo eliminate $p,$ we first solve the first equation for $p:$\n\n$$\np=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)\n$$\n\nThis is valid only for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le p\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nNext, let's substitute this expression for $p$ into the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =p\\operatorname{sin}⁡(p)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(p) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)\\cdot x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the explicit form of the singular solution is\n\n$$\ny=x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x)),\\,-1\\le x\\le 1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334457/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ddcff62-d052-51fd-9e2b-50358fa02de5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334457"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
